{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1560676-advancement-for-loners","id":1560676,"title":"Advancement for loners","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-06-17T07:14:18-07:00","id":1560676,"title":"Advancement for loners","content":"Due to circumstances\u2122, the Stargazer in my group will be separated from his Pack and Sept for an extended period of time, but I don't want to block advancement for the PC just because my plot spirits him away. I could handwave advancement and just make Renown permanent, but I would rather have something a little more integrated.<br /> <br /> So far I'm considering to let an Ancestor Spirit step in for Rite of Accomplishment, or having a Messenger Spirit turn up at the moot. It may help that the PC will be more or less directly on a mission under guidance of his tribal Totem, although I don't think Chimera would be directly concerned about his advancement.<br /> <br /> Advancing in Rank if it happens presents a problem with the challenge to a higher Rank. Again, having an Ancestor stand in may be an option, but I'm not sure I like that solution too much. I feel Rank is something that's more important to the Sept and should be known there.<br /> <br /> If you have any better ideas or handled a situation like that before, I'm thankful for any solutions you may have found.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-17T12:23:46-07:00","id":1560683,"title":"","content":"On the Renown side of thing: Rev and 20th addressed that the default assumption of the game is that temporary Renown gets rewarded primarily by the spirits some of whom are always watching. The books also provide that in exceptional circumstances the spirits can even award permanent Renown without the Rite of Accomplishment being performed. The spirits are technically responsible for powering the Rite in the first place.<br /> <br /> That said, Rank is not given that flexibility. Rank is earned from higher Ranking Garou. That said, Rank has no real restrictions on it mechanically. A Garou on a long quest can come back with lots of spirit granted Renown and start Challenging for Rank rapidly rather than the normal pace of &quot;get enough Renown, challenge for Rank, get more Renown, Rank again, repeat.&quot; Though you could allow a Garou to jump over Ranks without really contradicting anything in the book. If you leave your Sept for a Quest as a Fostern, and come path with Athro Renown... there's nothing explicit stopping you from challenging for Athro instead challening for Adren first, and then Athro. It's just Garou tradition that asks for existing high Rank Garou to make you jump through the hoops.<br /> <br /> So not letting them Rank up is only a problem if they need a Gift to solve a problem and don't have the Rank for it... which is just something you can avoid putting in the way as ST.<br /> <br /> Broadly though, there's a lot of variation on this by ST and table preference. How big of a problem this is depends on how pacing in your game is already going. Some groups play things in a way where it could take a year to get enough Renown to gain Rank, and others might allow Renown to come so fast you can Rank every month or two. Nobody is doing anything wrong here, the system is, well, not really structured to take individual group pacing into account.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T03:10:54-07:00","id":1560701,"title":"","content":"Even Gifts aren't a problem. Spirits <i><b>do </b></i>give higher level Gifts from time to time. A Garou that's lower Rank than they should precisely because of mission constraints seems right up in the alley of someone who would be given some leeway, as the spirits know their deeds and all.<br /> <br /> Depending on the nature of the mission, it's also possible to have other Garou involved, loners or from other Septs, able to recognize Rank and/or accept challenge.<br /> <br /> Also good to talk with the player. Sometimes you're overthinking a problem they don't want &quot;solved&quot;, or have their own expectations on what the solution should look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-19T10:19:19-07:00","id":1560758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1560676-advancement-for-loners?p=1560683#post1560683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Broadly though, there's a lot of variation on this by ST and table preference. How big of a problem this is depends on how pacing in your game is already going. Some groups play things in a way where it could take a year to get enough Renown to gain Rank, and others might allow Renown to come so fast you can Rank every month or two. Nobody is doing anything wrong here, the system is, well, not really structured to take individual group pacing into account.</div> </div> </div> </div>This group only plays once, maybe twice a year, but then in long sessions. I always give XP and Renown at the end because of the long interval, and the players can do advancement and housekeeping between sessions. So far I managed to keep it episodic enough to land on downtime for the characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1560676-advancement-for-loners?p=1560683#post1560683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Renown side of thing: Rev and 20th addressed that the default assumption of the game is that temporary Renown gets rewarded primarily by the spirits some of whom are always watching. The books also provide that in exceptional circumstances the spirits can even award permanent Renown without the Rite of Accomplishment being performed. The spirits are technically responsible for powering the Rite in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will be honest, playing out Rite of Accomplishment is super convenient for having an IC recap at the start of the session instead of just ST-dumping everything on the players. Keeping the active component would be nice in that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1560676-advancement-for-loners?p=1560683#post1560683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So not letting them Rank up is only a problem if they need a Gift to solve a problem and don't have the Rank for it... which is just something you can avoid putting in the way as ST.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1560676-advancement-for-loners?p=1560701#post1560701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even Gifts aren't a problem. Spirits <i><b>do </b></i>give higher level Gifts from time to time. A Garou that's lower Rank than they should precisely because of mission constraints seems right up in the alley of someone who would be given some leeway, as the spirits know their deeds and all.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Gift caps were my main concern with Rank. Looking back at it, it seems a bit strange that Gift caps are tied to Rank. I mean, I understand it from a game-design point, but the relationship between PC and Spirits should probably matter more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1560676-advancement-for-loners?p=1560701#post1560701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depending on the nature of the mission, it's also possible to have other Garou involved, loners or from other Septs, able to recognize Rank and/or accept challenge.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The group is going on a long umbral journey, random encounters with other Garou are possible but unlikely unless I provoke them. They will be mostly meeting Wraiths, Dreams, Spirits, and maybe a currently dead Mummy if I can pull it off. The Ancestor Spirit was the closest I could think of that wouldn't be too much out of place in most realms, hence the idea. But maybe I can replace that with a conveniently placed Silent Strider.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1560676-advancement-for-loners?p=1560701#post1560701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also good to talk with the player. Sometimes you're overthinking a problem they don't want &quot;solved&quot;, or have their own expectations on what the solution should look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. I'm holding off a bit to not spoil the 'abduction' twist for him, and it would be good to have a suggestion ready should he want it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-19T11:19:00-07:00","id":1560761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1560676-advancement-for-loners?p=1560758#post1560758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Gift caps were my main concern with Rank. Looking back at it, it seems a bit strange that Gift caps are tied to Rank. I mean, I understand it from a game-design point, but the relationship between PC and Spirits should probably matter more.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the game isn't entirely consistent, the gist of it is that neither the magic of the Gift comes from the spirit alone, nor the reason of the spirit is purely personal.<br /> <br /> Behind the whole structure of Gifts are ancient magical pacts establishing mutual obligations that define Gifts and Gift teaching. Pacts with specific spirits, pacts with choirs, pacts with the Umbra itself.<br /> <br /> Those are the ancient frameworks that make the whole exchange possible in the first place. Without them, Gifts don't exist. Spirits have their Charms and that's it. And they have no reason to help strangers in exchange of minor rituals outside the framework that gives power to said rituals.<br /> <br /> So, when your PC gives chiminage to a spirit in exchange for a Gift, they're not making a small personal favor to be taught a trick in return. They are reenacting an ancient ceremony by the firsts of the Stargazers, stepping in the very shoes of Klaital to honor and reinforce their oaths to the totem and to the Incarnae of that spirit's choir, and it is the symbolism of this old story resonating across the Umbra in the era of Evernow where those actions happen that awakens in the character the power of the Gift.<br /> <br /> Add to that that spirits aren't just supernatural beings, they're meaning made manifest, and so even their personal relationships aren't &quot;personal&quot; in a normal sense. Rank Defines the very identity of the Garou in the relationship, and to the spirit this identity is reality more than material context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-19T11:26:58-07:00","id":1560763,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit confused. If the group is going on a long Umbra quest, even with one of them getting separated for plot reasons, aren't they all going to have the same issues with Renown and Rank advancement? If they're all going to be away from the Sept and easy access to the Rite of Accomplishment and Garou to challenge for Rank, then none of them will advance along those lines faster than anyone else. Doing the Rite at the start of the session when they all get back still works as the recap function as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-19T11:43:23-07:00","id":1560766,"title":"","content":"Oh sorry, I completely failed to mentioned that it's a mixed group. The Stargazer, a werespider, two sorcerers. The latter will have ample opportunities to advance their Paths, and the Ananasi has a Rite to let her access her Sylie through dreaming.<br /> <br /> The Pack and Sept of the Stargazer are Background NPCs; when we started out, the player wasn't sure about his character and didn't want to start as a Ronin.<br /> <br /> Also, thank you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> for the lore refresher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}